  "evidence": "The selected assembly provides its published GL doubling proposition by a local proof. The common-superlattice series and Borel spherical series were checked at the suppliers below. The worked coefficients were recomputed independently by enumerating the subgroups of orders 2 and 4 in (Z/4)^2.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "SPE-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "Counting the intermediate lattices gives the split normalizer",
      "anchor": "lifts-split-euler",
      "statement": "Fix the endpoint lattice Λ=gΛ₀ with elementary divisors d_i. For each intermediate H containing Λ and Λ₀, passage through H has length Σ|d_i|+2 length(H/(Λ+Λ₀)). Its generating series over H equals X^{Σ|d_i|} times ∏_{i=0}^{a−1}(1−q^i X²)^{-1}. Removing this multiplicity gives the polynomial ∏(1−q^i X²) in the local doubling sum.",
      "hypotheses": "The local field is nonarchimedean with a discrete valuation, lattice ring O and residue-field cardinality q. The endpoint lattice has full rank a. The geometric series converges when |q^i X²|<1 at each i.",
